<!--Post: 607--><!--Time: 1090901851-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST607"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 26, 2004 - 9:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t believe this theory, and it&#39;s very cynical, but given human nature, I can see it possibly happening. <BR> <BR>What is the city of Wichita&#39;s largest source of income? It would have to be WSU. I happen to believe there are <i>many</i> BTK victims &#40;like four or five&#41; which certain peolpe knew were the work of BTK but kept quiet because when there&#39;s a serial killer in town, families tend to not send their daughters&#39; in harms way. In other words, to keep the WSU revenue flowing, I can see the powers-that-be being close-mouthed about probable BTK victims&#39; for the sake of WSU. I repeat, I don&#39;t believe this, but I&#39;ve seen enough corruption in my life to know <BR>that the above is possible.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 607-->
<!--Post: 611--><!--Time: 1090905897-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST611"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Laoise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Laoise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 26, 2004 - 10:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Actually Boeing is a HUGE source of income for wichita. WSU really isnt that big a deal around here... <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 611-->
<!--Post: 616--><!--Time: 1090950678-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST616"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 27, 2004 - 10:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Excellent. Thanks, Laoise. And Boeing was well established in Wichita in 1974? <BR> <BR>I&#39;m not really going so much for a theory here as looking for a reason the police have done so little! <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 616-->
<!--Post: 623--><!--Time: 1090964233-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST623"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Laoise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Laoise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 27, 2004 - 2:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->yes im pretty sure boeing was well established then....then again i was all of 7 yrs old and living in hawaii in &#39;74!  lol  we moved here in &#39;76 but it seems to me boeing was here then. keep in mind that wichita is the air capital for a reason! ;&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 623-->
<!--Post: 628--><!--Time: 1090973968-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST628"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 27, 2004 - 5:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Glad to hear it, Laoise. That ends an ugly thought <BR>I read in March or April on one of the other BTK boards. I don&#39;t remember which board it was, except that it was wild and many BTK legends were accepted as fact. I was only nine during the two <BR>1974 BTK attacks and living in Annandale, VA, which I miss terribly; it became too expensive to live in Fairfax County and I had to move to western Maryland.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 628-->
<!--Post: 647--><!--Time: 1091127728-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST647"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Warren_b<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Warren_b<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, July 29, 2004 - 12:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think Boeing made B-29s during WWII in Wichita.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 647-->
<!--Post: 648--><!--Time: 1091140336-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST648"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, July 29, 2004 - 3:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Warren, thanks. A huge, established corporation, a <BR>notable State University. Maybe the police have a complete plan, which includes telling the public &#40;comparatively&#41; very little. If the police might say as much, perhaps the palpable frustration among the public regarding the police&#39;s attitude would decrease. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 648-->
<!--Post: 651--><!--Time: 1091196100-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST651"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Matt<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Matt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, July 30, 2004 - 7:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->didn&#39;t Warren _B used to be a fireman at Boeing ?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 651-->
</table></td></tr></table>
